  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "DeGeorge entered business through the industrial platform assembled by his father, Lawrence J. DeGeorge, and developed substantial operating experience at connector manufacturer Amphenol. He progressed from chief financial officer to president and joined his father in an offer to take parent company LPL Technologies private. That foundation gave him an unusually strong start in leveraged acquisitions and communications infrastructure.\n\nAs chief executive of several LPL investment entities, DeGeorge directed capital into telecommunications and biotechnology. His holdings included control of Advance Display Technologies and a substantial investment in European fibre operator CompleTel. He was also chairman and majority shareholder of data-centre company Cervalis, where he secured expansion financing. His later work includes the LDG & LPR Charitable Foundation, which supports children’s health, education and family services.",
    "html": "<p>DeGeorge entered business through the industrial platform assembled by his father, Lawrence J. DeGeorge, and developed substantial operating experience at connector manufacturer Amphenol. He progressed from chief financial officer to president and joined his father in an offer to take parent company LPL Technologies private. That foundation gave him an unusually strong start in leveraged acquisitions and communications infrastructure.</p>\r\n<p>As chief executive of several LPL investment entities, DeGeorge directed capital into telecommunications and biotechnology. His holdings included control of Advance Display Technologies and a substantial investment in European fibre operator CompleTel. He was also chairman and majority shareholder of data-centre company Cervalis, where he secured expansion financing. His later work includes the LDG &amp; LPR Charitable Foundation, which supports children’s health, education and family services.</p>\r\n",
